From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 07:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: exynos9820: Add CMU_PERIC1

Add the clock controller of the second peripheral block: 16 user muxes, 15
dividers and 72 gates, all transcribed from the vendor clock tables.

The register offsets, the bit positions and the parents come from those
tables.  What does not come from them, and is a decision of this port, is
which clocks may not be gated when nobody claims them: the bus ports and
the PCLK of the controller itself, the same rule the blocks above follow.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c | 609 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 609 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c
index 3ea1e9a631c..79a99c81fe7 100644
